The stream included edge bars and isolated/motif colors, but the sole supplied demo that changed cells changed only two adjacent 5s to 6s (demo 1: rows 2–3, column 1 in zero-based coordinates); demos 2–4 changed only small portions: demo 2 changed three 7s in a 7-bar to 4s, demo 3 changed a 3x2 patch of 8s to 7s, and demo 4 recolored a compact 5-shape to 6. These are distinct local recolorings, not evidence for projecting broad edge rays. Repeated submissions that altered a guessed 3-color edge pattern failed, illustrating the need to fit a selector or relation to all demos before transfer.

Operational lesson: compute each demo's exact delta, including changed old/new colors and unchanged candidates; do not infer common mechanics just from edge bars or marker presence. If hypotheses remain unvalidated, a demo is useful only if its geometry discriminates them. Do not submit a rule unsupported by exact demo replay. This note does not establish a solved transformation for this task.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-3/play/users/u070/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-task-delta-inference/references/session-dabb45d0-review.md"}

